From 236563c95a8a5b948288cc77b95f32697fdb9ba0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Doctor Logix <doctor.logix@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:29:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 151/162] media: i2c: ov16a1q: use the binned mode, BGGR

The OV16A1Q is a Quad Bayer sensor. A full-resolution frame of an
SMPTE chart (devices145) has each colour in 2x2 blocks, greens on the
anti-diagonal; averaged block by block and read as BGGR, the bars
come out in their order. That readout needs a remosaic before any
Bayer pipeline can use it.

Use the stock 2x2 binned mode instead: 2304x1728 at 30 fps, the same
field of view, ordinary Bayer at the block order. It sends 800 Mbit/s
per lane (MIPI period register 0x4837 = 20, PLL multiplier 225 halved
against 198 for 0x4837 = 11 in the full mode), a 400 MHz link clock.

(cherry picked from commit 81e5b80422f1c4a7da9a68a201ea00beb7880f73)
